        "eyebrow": "Virtual staging near you",
        "heading": "Virtual Staging Los Angeles, CA",
        "lede": "Virtual staging is digital home staging for listing photos: an interior designer places realistic 3D furniture and decor into photos of empty rooms, so buyers can see scale, flow and lifestyle before they tour. LA listings sell a lifestyle before they sell square footage, and Bella's Los Angeles virtual staging — plus day-to-twilight editing — comes back in 24 to 48 hours, from {price:virtual-staging} a photo.",
        "cta_label": "Stage my listing — from {price:virtual-staging}",
        "cta_link": "/products/virtual-staging",
        "alt_label": "Browse the lookbook",
        "alt_link": "/pages/lookbook",
        "city": "Los Angeles",
        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging matters in the Los Angeles market",
        "market_text": "<p>Los Angeles buyers are as image-literate as any in the country — they scroll past anything that doesn't look like the homes they see on Instagram and Zillow's front page. An empty Spanish bungalow or a bare new build in the hills leaves the lifestyle to the imagination, and in LA the lifestyle is the product.</p><p>Indoor-outdoor space is where LA listings win: staged patios, decks and yards routinely out-click staged living rooms. Our home staging covers exteriors too, and our day-to-dusk editing turns a flat afternoon exterior into the golden-hour shot that anchors the listing.</p><p>Los Angeles is also a market where physical staging is genuinely expensive and genuinely slow — coastal and hillside listings can run thousands a month, and scheduling a crew up a canyon road is its own problem. Staging the photos removes the logistics and fixes the cost at {price:virtual-staging} a photo, whether the listing closes in ten days or ninety.</p><p>That makes the listing photos the first showing for most buyers — 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search, according to the National Association of Realtors. In a competitive market full of luxury listings and investment properties, virtually staged photos help Los Angeles listings stand out in the scroll and give buyers a reason to book the tour.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Los Angeles virtual staging, pocket by pocket",
        "local_text": "<p>From Silver Lake creative contemporaries to Westside family traditionals, our designers furnish to the buyer each pocket attracts. Every image is MLS-ready, disclosed as virtually staged, and delivered in 24 to 48 hours.</p><p>Architectural listings get handled as architecture. A Spanish revival, a mid-century post-and-beam and a new spec build each want a different furniture vocabulary, and staging that ignores the house tends to read as a stock room dropped into someone's photo.</p><p>Files are sized for CRMLS and The MLS (CLAW), so the same set uploads wherever you list, and every order ships with AB 723 disclosure guidance and full usage rights. Volume discounts apply automatically — 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "Silver Lake, Los Feliz, Echo Park, Venice, Santa Monica, Brentwood, Studio City, Sherman Oaks, Pasadena, Hollywood Hills"
      }
    },
